WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.629 --> 00:00:03.330
(speaking in foreign language)

00:00:03.330 --> 00:00:05.520
- [Narrator] This documentary
by Russian State Media

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:09.090
praises a private military
company called Wagner.

00:00:09.090 --> 00:00:11.460
The paramilitary group
operating in Ukraine

00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:14.340
has been getting a lot
of positive coverage.

00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:16.820
All this despite private
military organizations

00:00:16.820 --> 00:00:19.560
being illegal in Russia.

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:21.390
Just before the invasion of Ukraine,

00:00:21.390 --> 00:00:24.154
the Russian president denied any ties.

00:00:24.154 --> 00:00:26.760
(speaking in foreign language)

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:28.756
Kiev has accused Wagner of war crimes.

00:00:28.756 --> 00:00:31.920
Now, as Moscow loses ground in Ukraine,

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:34.526
the company is gaining prominence.

00:00:34.526 --> 00:00:35.359
(object banging)

00:00:35.359 --> 00:00:37.110
News reports and social media accounts

00:00:37.110 --> 00:00:40.560
show Wagner's men leading
attacks in Eastern Ukraine,

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:42.390
tapping prisoners to fight

00:00:42.390 --> 00:00:46.050
and sending threatening messages
to the Kremlin's opponents.

00:00:46.050 --> 00:00:47.670
Here's how the secretive company

00:00:47.670 --> 00:00:51.048
has come to take on a
semi-official role in Ukraine.

00:00:51.048 --> 00:00:53.100
(gentle music)

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:56.220
Formed in 2014 to fight
in Ukraine back then,

00:00:56.220 --> 00:00:57.660
Wagner has since operated

00:00:57.660 --> 00:01:00.579
in Syria and several African countries.

00:01:00.579 --> 00:01:03.240
Since the spring, it's been indispensable

00:01:03.240 --> 00:01:05.340
for Moscow's invasion of Ukraine.

00:01:05.340 --> 00:01:07.200
That's according to Ukrainian commanders

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:09.630
who detected its presence early on.

00:01:09.630 --> 00:01:12.360
After Russia's main
offensive stalled in May,

00:01:12.360 --> 00:01:15.240
Wagner managed to take
the town of Popasna,

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:16.800
paving the way for the Russian army

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:19.313
to take several strategic cities.

00:01:19.313 --> 00:01:21.390
Recently, the group has been fighting

00:01:21.390 --> 00:01:23.804
for the eastern city of Bakhmut.

00:01:23.804 --> 00:01:28.110
(speaking in foreign language)

00:01:28.110 --> 00:01:30.690
As Wagner slowly advances toward the city,

00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:33.840
Russian propaganda has been
amplifying its importance,

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:36.030
anticipating that President Vladimir Putin

00:01:36.030 --> 00:01:37.410
could tout a rare victory

00:01:37.410 --> 00:01:39.993
after a series of losses and setbacks.

00:01:41.520 --> 00:01:43.661
But Wagner's services come at a cost.

00:01:43.661 --> 00:01:48.060
The group has been losing about
10% to 15% of its fighters

00:01:48.060 --> 00:01:51.840
on an average mission in
Ukraine as dead or wounded.

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:53.070
That's according to an estimate

00:01:53.070 --> 00:01:56.070
by a former Ukrainian
intelligence official.

00:01:56.070 --> 00:01:57.630
Wagner's fighters are paid better

00:01:57.630 --> 00:01:59.550
than the regular Russian troops,

00:01:59.550 --> 00:02:01.410
with an advertised starting monthly pay

00:02:01.410 --> 00:02:05.582
of around $3,500 compared to $2,700

00:02:05.582 --> 00:02:08.613
that Moscow pays its
soldiers fighting in Ukraine.

00:02:09.540 --> 00:02:11.610
And recently, the company has resorted

00:02:11.610 --> 00:02:14.860
to unconventional measures
to find new recruits.

00:02:14.860 --> 00:02:16.950
(speaking in foreign language)

00:02:16.950 --> 00:02:19.260
In September, a video circulating online

00:02:19.260 --> 00:02:20.700
showed a man recruiting inmates

00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:22.620
for Wagner in a Russian prison.

00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:26.370
The news agency Storyful was
able to confirm the location.

00:02:26.370 --> 00:02:27.480
A social media account

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:29.670
affiliated with Wagner identified the man

00:02:29.670 --> 00:02:33.540
as Yevgeny Prigozhin,
Wagner's owner and leader.

00:02:33.540 --> 00:02:36.401
Prigozhin has said he has
visited several penal colonies

00:02:36.401 --> 00:02:38.400
but he declined to answer our questions

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:42.060
on the recruitment of inmates
and Wagner's role in the war.

00:02:42.060 --> 00:02:44.820
Enlist prisoners comes as
Moscow is trying to balance

00:02:44.820 --> 00:02:47.610
its highly unpopular mobilization efforts

00:02:47.610 --> 00:02:49.830
with its need for troops.

00:02:49.830 --> 00:02:51.300
Russian human rights activists

00:02:51.300 --> 00:02:53.730
estimated that at least 15,000 inmates

00:02:53.730 --> 00:02:56.823
had been recruited to fight
in Ukraine by mid-October.

00:02:57.750 --> 00:02:59.760
Recruiting inmates has another advantage

00:02:59.760 --> 00:03:02.340
as the official troops morale falters.

00:03:02.340 --> 00:03:04.380
Consequences for refusing to fight

00:03:04.380 --> 00:03:06.672
are more severe for them.

00:03:06.672 --> 00:03:10.770
(speaking in foreign language)

00:03:10.770 --> 00:03:13.260
That message was reinforced in November.

00:03:13.260 --> 00:03:16.080
A Wagner linked social
media account shared a video

00:03:16.080 --> 00:03:18.529
purporting to show group members

00:03:18.529 --> 00:03:20.640
killing one of their
own with a sledgehammer.

00:03:20.640 --> 00:03:22.320
The victim had identified himself

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:24.780
as a former convict who
tried to switch sides

00:03:24.780 --> 00:03:26.670
and fight for Ukraine.

00:03:26.670 --> 00:03:28.530
The authenticity of that footage

00:03:28.530 --> 00:03:31.077
which we are not showing
here, couldn't be verified

00:03:31.077 --> 00:03:34.650
but Prigozhin separately
said the man was a traitor.

00:03:34.650 --> 00:03:37.440
Days later, Wagner used
a sledgehammer again.

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:40.170
This time, the group sent one
to the European parliament

00:03:40.170 --> 00:03:44.640
after the EU branded Russia,
a state sponsor of terrorism.

00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:46.740
The Russian Ministry of
Defense didn't respond

00:03:46.740 --> 00:03:47.970
to our request for comment

00:03:47.970 --> 00:03:50.463
on Wagner's growing prominence in Ukraine.

00:03:52.290 --> 00:03:55.290
Wagner's rise comes at a time
when nationalist hardliners

00:03:55.290 --> 00:03:56.310
in Russia are calling

00:03:56.310 --> 00:03:59.730
for tougher methods to turn
the tide in Moscow's favor.

00:03:59.730 --> 00:04:01.680
And the mercenaries activities in Ukraine

00:04:01.680 --> 00:04:04.517
are welcomed by pro-war
critics of the Kremlin.

00:04:04.517 --> 00:04:07.272
Military analysts in the
West say the expanded role

00:04:07.272 --> 00:04:09.398
for an organization accused of war crimes

00:04:09.398 --> 00:04:12.480
and one that is recruiting
convicted criminals,

00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:13.650
is a telling indicator

00:04:13.650 --> 00:04:16.650
of the perilous state
of Putin's war machine.

00:04:16.650 --> 00:04:18.120
In December, Putin said

00:04:18.120 --> 00:04:21.033
that the military campaign
in Ukraine was going well.

